      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day, under medical supervision). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens that may be what you meant:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** for typical analgesia.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. This may be the source of the \"1600\" figure.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1,600 mg four times daily is intended and why. I'll enter the order once that's settled. If you do want the higher dose, I'll add a note to the order recording that it was confirmed."
      }
     ],
